  "If a course should not be built, or a project is not ours to take, we say so at the first conversation. Where we can, we point you to someone better placed.": "若某门课程不该开发，或某个项目不宜由我们承接，我们会在第一次交谈时如实相告。在力所能及之处，我们会为您引荐更合适的人选。",
  "If the list above looks daunting, that is by design.": "若上面的清单看起来令人望而生畏，那正是有意为之。",
  "If you have read this far, the proposal is simple. Send us a note, in plain words, about the work you have in mind. We will reply within two working days, in the same plain manner.": "如果您读到了这里，那么提议很简单。请用平实的话语，把您心中的项目写信告诉我们。我们会在两个工作日内，以同样平实的方式回复。",
  "If you operate as a registered training provider, or intend to become one, three things will decide whether the business holds. Approval decides whether you have a product at all. A course the Skills and Workforce Development Agency (SWDA), formerly SkillsFuture Singapore (SSG), has not endorsed carries no subsidy, and few learners will be willing to pay for the full fee. Curriculum decides what you then have to build. Once approval is granted, you are bound to the course you described, and the materials and assessments must answer to it. Audit decides whether you keep what you have. A provider whose records diverge from its submissions can forfeit the approval it worked to obtain.": "若您以注册培训机构的身份运营，或有意成为一家，有三件事将决定这门生意能否立得住。审批决定您是否拥有产品。一门未获技能与劳动力发展局（SWDA，前身为新加坡技能创前程／SSG）背书的课程不带任何补贴，鲜有学员愿意支付全额费用。课程开发决定您接下来要构建什么。一旦获得审批，您便受制于自己所描述的那门课程，材料与评估都必须与之相符。审计决定您能否守住已有的一切。若一家机构的记录与其提交内容出现偏离，便可能失去它辛苦争取来的审批。",
  "If you skip the manual, it is because…": "如果你跳过说明书不看，那是因为……",
